      "exact_print_body_reading": "an-tik'wi-ti (קַדְמָה, kadmāh, from קדם, kādham, “to precede in time,” “to be old”): In Ezk 16 55; 36 11, rendered “former”; in Ps 129 6, “before.” Trᵈ “antiquity” only in Isa 23 7 to indicate the primeval age of Tyre, which Strabo terms, “after Sidon,” the oldest Phoen city. Delitzsch renders it “whose origin is from the days of the olden time.”"
